# Artworks from the Met
// Artworks of the Metropolitan Museum of Art, found by what you type:  a wall of pictures that goes on as you scroll.
// Every thing it shows is in MetArtworks.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
// so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
// Its search answers only ids:  each artwork is read from its own address as it's drawn, and no others.
// An artwork with no picture is left out:  the wall draws more as you scroll, so a short screen fills from the next ones.

met artworks is an app
	its "search" is text
	when creating it
		set its search to "sunflowers"
	its "found" is every artwork matching the search
		// What the Met finds for the search, looking at all of each artwork:  ids only, each read as it's drawn

	to try (words as text)
		set its search to words

	to draw it
		<container>
			<stack spacing="lg">
				<form value={it}>
					<stack spacing="sm">
						<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="center" justify="between" spacing="sm">
							<header size="large">Artworks from the Met</header>
							<search name="search" parameter="art" icon="search" placeholder="A title, an artist, a subject" aria-label="Search the Met" />
						</stack>
						<toolbar appearance="secondary" size="small" aria-label="Try a search">
							<text slot="title" size="small" color="grey">Try</text>
							<item onClick={try "sunflowers"}>Sunflowers</item>
							<item onClick={try "van gogh"}>Van Gogh</item>
							<item onClick={try "hokusai"}>Hokusai</item>
							<item onClick={try "armor"}>Armor</item>
							<item onClick={try "cats"}>Cats</item>
							<item onClick={try "egypt"}>Egypt</item>
						</toolbar>
					</stack>
				</form>
				<for its found as="cards" layout="mosaic" columns="4" doubling loading="Asking the Met" failed="The Met can't be reached just now." empty="The Met has nothing for that." />
				<text size="small" color="grey" paragraph>
					From <link link="https://metmuseum.github.io">the Met Museum's API</link>, each artwork asked for as it's shown.  Press a picture to turn it over.
				</text>
			</stack>
		</container>

# An artwork
// A card that turns over:  its picture on the front, what the Met knows of it on the back.
// Only what's in the public domain has a picture:  the rest draw nothing, so the wall is all pictures.

an artwork
	to draw it
		if its primary image small
			<shape class="artwork" direction="over" flip-on="click" aria-label={its title}>
				<side>
					<card fluid>
						<image src={its primary image small} alt={its title} />
						<content>
							<header size="small">{its title}</header>
							<meta>{its artist display name}</meta>
							<meta>{its object date}</meta>
						</content>
					</card>
				</side>
				<side>{draw the about card of it}</side>
			</shape>

	to draw its about card
		// What the Met knows of it:  the back of its card
		<card fluid>
			<content>
				<header size="small">{its title}</header>
				<meta>{its artist display name} · {its object date}</meta>
				<description>
					<text paragraph>{its medium}</text>
					<text paragraph>{its dimensions}</text>
					<text paragraph color="grey">{its department} · {its credit line}</text>
				</description>
			</content>
			<extra>
				<link link={its object url} target="_blank">On the Met's own pages</link>
			</extra>
		</card>
